{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 42, "timestamp": 1793213874, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "env": {"SHELL": null, "TERM": null}, "title": "PR 714 web stop PID owner - before/after"}
[0.368466, "o", "$ # PR #714 — peasant web stop must only signal its own web server (issue #671)\r\n$ # A stale web-<port>.pid can name ANY reused PID. Plant a harmless\r\n$ # stand-in (sleep 300, started by this script) in a fake PID file.\r\n"]
[1.411981, "o", "\r\n================ BEFORE: develop (be2bc57f) ================\r\n"]
[1.46003, "o", "$ sleep 300 &  # stand-in PID 60650, planted in web-18693.pid\r\n"]
[1.719078, "o", "    PID COMMAND         COMMAND\r\n  60650 sleep           sleep 300\r\n"]
[1.729251, "o", "$ peasant-before web stop --port 18693\r\n"]
[2.99613, "o", "HTTP shutdown failed: Post \"http://localhost:18693/api/v1/shutdown\": dial tcp [::1]:18693: connect: connection refused, falling back to SIGTERM\r\n"]
[3.010453, "o", "Sent SIGTERM to PID 60650\r\n"]
[3.058626, "o", "exit=0\r\n"]
[4.160227, "o", ">>> stand-in 60650 was KILLED by web stop on develop (BUG, #671)\r\n\r\n================ AFTER: PR #714 head (47b14407, rebased) ================\r\n"]
[4.256882, "o", "$ sleep 300 &  # stand-in PID 60710, planted in web-18694.pid\r\n"]
[4.565092, "o", "    PID COMMAND         COMMAND\r\n  60710 sleep           sleep 300\r\n"]
[4.5956, "o", "$ peasant-after web stop --port 18694\r\n"]
[6.922828, "o", "HTTP shutdown failed: Post \"http://localhost:18694/api/v1/shutdown\": dial tcp [::1]:18694: connect: connection refused, falling back to SIGTERM\r\nError: stale PID file /home/hatch/workspace/pr-evidence/pr-714/evidence/demo-scratch/after-home/.local/state/peasant/web-18694.pid: PID 60710 is not a peasant web server on port 18694, so nothing was signalled; the file was removed. If a server is still running, find it with your process list and stop it there\r\n"]
[7.06356, "o", "exit=1\r\n"]
[8.144594, "o", ">>> stand-in 60710 is STILL ALIVE — nothing was signalled (FIXED)\r\n$ ls $XDG_STATE_HOME/peasant/  # stale PID file was removed\r\n"]
[8.199044, "o", "# now killing my own stand-in myself:\r\n"]
[8.256035, "o", "stand-in cleaned up\r\n\r\n================ LEGIT PATH: real server start/stop (PR binary) ================\r\n"]
[8.357053, "o", "$ peasant-after web start --no-browser --port 18695\r\n"]
[12.887516, "o", "Peasant web dashboard running at http://localhost:18695\r\nTo stop the server, run:\r\n  peasant web stop\r\n\r\nIf the server becomes unresponsive, the process ID (60820)\r\nis saved at /home/hatch/workspace/pr-evidence/pr-714/evidence/demo-scratch/legit-home/.local/state/peasant/web-18695.pid\r\n"]
[12.964229, "o", "start exit=0\r\n"]
[14.674019, "o", "health check HTTP 200\r\n"]
[14.766944, "o", "web-18695.pid\r\n$ peasant-after web stop --port 18695\r\n"]
[15.353675, "o", "Peasant web dashboard shutting down\r\n"]
[15.466088, "o", "stop exit=0\r\n"]
[16.770671, "o", ">>> server stopped — port 18695 no longer answers\r\n\r\n$ # DONE: before = stand-in killed; after = stand-in untouched, real server still stops.\r\n"]
